            <div xml:id="d1155">

                <pb facs="0954" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.113/911.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-09-07T12:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 7, 1912—12
                        noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following to Consul Dye, at Douglas, to-day: [Quotes Department’s telegram of
                    September 7, 1912, 12 noon.]</p>
                <p>The arms and ammunition are being forwarded to the consul for the use of
                    seriously endangered Americans for the protection of their lives and property.
                    Immediately make all necessary arrangements with the Mexican Government for the
                    entry of these arms and ammunition, so that there will be no delay upon
                    arrival.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Adee.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
